1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,062
Reviewing a protein variant requires more than a model score.

2
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:11,093
BioPilot Atlas connects residue checks, bounded computation, and inspectable evidence through MCP.

3
00:00:11,243 --> 00:00:19,582
This local draft uses edited still captures from a saved real run, with synthetic narration, not a
continuous screen recording.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,223
The example reviews a public Lipase A reference using full reference, one based positions.

5
00:00:26,373 --> 00:00:30,242
The registered scoring context is the complete sequence.

6
00:00:30,392 --> 00:00:34,766
Code protects the catalytic sites and enforces approved limits.

7
00:00:34,916 --> 00:00:42,469
The language model cannot grant itself permission, change the reference, or silently convert residue
numbering.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,694
The saved execution used Muse Spark through the controlled Python host.

9
00:00:49,844 --> 00:00:54,557
Meta requested target validation, then the permitted scoring tool.

10
00:00:54,707 --> 00:01:01,256
The MCP server checked the requests and local ESM computed sequence preferences on the CPU.

11
00:01:01,406 --> 00:01:07,224
The run finished with a separate explanation, while code generated the candidate ranking.

12
00:01:07,374 --> 00:01:10,748
The original execution took forty seconds.

13
00:01:10,898 --> 00:01:15,162
Viewing these saved results now sends no provider request.

14
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,254
Here is a separate local guard check, captured during submission preparation.

15
00:01:25,404 --> 00:01:31,112
The valid variant passes, while a substitution at the protected serine is blocked.

16
00:01:31,262 --> 00:01:35,511
This is actual command output, rendered from its receipt.

17
00:01:35,661 --> 00:01:40,079
It is not a new Meta conversation or an adaptive model recovery.

18
00:01:40,229 --> 00:01:47,398
The division of responsibility is explicit: Meta requests tools, and code enforces constraints.

19
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,719
The viewer displays the saved ranked candidates and their ESM scores.

20
00:01:54,869 --> 00:01:57,977
The numbers come directly from the artifact.

21
00:01:58,127 --> 00:02:01,966
One common score policy applies to every candidate.

22
00:02:02,116 --> 00:02:06,330
The retained model and reference hashes make the result inspectable.

23
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:11,873
Actual provider cost remains unknown; a reservation is not an invoice.

24
00:02:12,023 --> 00:02:18,976
ESM preferences do not establish thermal stability, activity, solubility, or retained function.

25
00:02:19,126 --> 00:02:22,510
Atom geometry also remains unverified.

26
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,443
This demonstration establishes a saved working integration and tested local guards.

27
00:02:30,593 --> 00:02:35,337
It does not establish biological improvement or a general time saving.

28
00:02:35,487 --> 00:02:41,300
A controlled manual, fixed, and Meta workflow comparison has not been measured.

29
00:02:41,450 --> 00:02:44,589
No experimental validation is claimed.

30
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,200
BioPilot contributes reusable guarded MCP tools and an inspectable Meta workflow.

31
00:02:50,350 --> 00:02:53,769
Earlier design work and external models remain credited.

32
00:02:53,919 --> 00:02:59,592
The repository, video access, eligibility, and final submission still need their own review.

